{"builder":"Goal: one pull request for issue https://github.com/o/greet-cli/issues/12 (--shout flag) that meets these acceptance lines:\n1. node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\n2. without --shout the output is unchanged\n3. docs/index.md documents --shout\n4. after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\n\nCurrent state: bin/greet.js takes the first argument not starting with `--` as the name and prints `greeting(name)` from src/greet.js (`Hello, <name>!`). Today `--shout` is silently ignored: `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints `Hello, Ada!`. Tests are in test/greet.test.js and run with `npm test` (`node --test`). docs/index.md is the docs page; .github/workflows/pages.yml publishes the docs/ directory to GitHub Pages on every push to main.\n\nSteps:\n1. In bin/greet.js, detect `--shout` anywhere in the arguments (before or after the name). When present, print the whole greeting line upper-cased, e.g. `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline. Keep the name parsing as is, so `--shout` is never taken as the name.\n2. Without `--shout`, keep the output byte for byte as now: `node bin/greet.js Ada` prints `Hello, Ada!\\n` with exit code 0, and `node bin/greet.js` with no name still writes `usage: greet <name>` to stderr and exits 2. You may mention `--shout` in the usage text only if you also leave the no-name case's exit code at 2; the simplest choice is to leave the usage text alone.\n3. Add tests to test/greet.test.js: one for `--shout Ada` giving `HELLO, ADA!\\n`, one for `Ada --shout` giving the same, and keep the existing `Ada` test giving `Hello, Ada!\\n`. Run `npm test` and make sure all pass.\n4. Update docs/index.md: add a usage line `node bin/greet.js --shout <name>` and a sentence saying it prints the greeting in upper case (e.g. `HELLO, <NAME>!`). The literal text `--shout` must appear in the file.\n5. Line 4 can only be met after the PR is merged to main and the pages workflow deploys docs/. Do not change .github/workflows/pages.yml unless it is needed for docs/index.md to be published. Note that https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ currently returns HTTP 404, so the site may not be published (for example, Pages not turned on in the repository settings). You cannot fix that from the PR; in the PR description, say that line 4 is a post-merge check and that the Pages site currently returns 404, so someone may need to enable GitHub Pages (source: GitHub Actions) for the pages workflow to publish it.\n6. Open one pull request with these changes, referencing issue #12.","verifier":"Verify the pull request for issue https://github.com/o/greet-cli/issues/12 against its acceptance lines. Run every command from the repository root at the PR head, after `npm test` (run it once first and note the result; it is context, not a check). One check per expect line, in order.\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\"\nRun:\n  node bin/greet.js --shout Ada; echo rc=$?\nPASS: stdout is exactly `HELLO, ADA!` (the normal greeting `Hello, Ada!` in upper case) followed by a newline, and rc=0.\nFAIL: any other output (e.g. `Hello, Ada!`, mixed case, the name missing or replaced by `--shout`), or a nonzero exit code.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"without --shout the output is unchanged\"\nRun:\n  node bin/greet.js Ada; echo rc=$?\n  node bin/greet.js \"Ada Lovelace\"; echo rc=$?\n  node bin/greet.js; echo rc=$?\nBefore the change these print, respectively: `Hello, Ada!` with rc=0; `Hello, Ada Lovelace!` with rc=0; `usage: greet <name>` on stderr with rc=2.\nPASS: all three give exactly that output and exit code.\nFAIL: any difference in text, case, trailing newline, stream, or exit code.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"docs/index.md documents --shout\"\nRun:\n  grep -n -e '--shout' docs/index.md; echo rc=$?\nand read docs/index.md.\nPASS: grep finds at least one line (rc=0) and the file tells the reader what `--shout` does (prints the greeting in upper case).\nFAIL: rc=1 (no mention), or `--shout` is mentioned without saying what it does.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\"\nThis line is about the live site after the PR is merged; it cannot be satisfied at the PR head alone. First find out whether the PR is merged (e.g. `gh pr view <number> --json state,mergedAt`) and, if merged, whether the pages workflow run on main after the merge succeeded (`gh run list --workflow pages.yml --branch main --limit 3`). Then run:\n  curl -sS -L -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\\n' https://o.github.io/greet-cli/\n  curl -sS -L https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ | grep -c -e '--shout'; echo rc=$?\nPASS: the PR is merged and the published page returns HTTP 200 and its content contains `--shout` (grep count ≥ 1, rc=0).\nFAIL: otherwise. If the PR is not merged yet, report FAIL with the reason \"not verifiable before merge\", and include the HTTP status you saw (at the time this brief was written the page returned 404), so it is clear the check is pending rather than broken by the code.\n\nAdvisory (not part of PASS/FAIL):\n- Also try `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` — it should match check 1's output if the flag works in any position.\n- Look for tests in test/greet.test.js covering both the shout and plain paths, and check that `npm test` passes.\n- Note any change to .github/workflows/pages.yml and whether it still publishes docs/ on push to main."}